The supplied float semantics explicitly anticipates this task: subtraction, `abs`, and `<` are opaque but fixed symbolic primitives under `kprove`, with concrete LLVM rules under `krun`. I’ll implement an index-based double `while` loop with a Boolean accumulator. That avoids early-return control effects and gives two clean symbolic loop invariants covering every pair `i < j` over an arbitrary finite list.
