The first connection attempt did not progress because fixed semantic functions do not constructor-split a completely abstract `ValSeq`. I’m restating the same universal theorem over the necessarily nonempty constructor case—valid indexing already implies nonempty—and letting the circularity induct on the tail after each positive-index step.
apply patch
