codex
The bridge-free indexing theorem cannot be made to constructor-split the fixed semantic helper on an abstract sequence, so under Gate A I’m removing that proof extension rather than trusting it. I’m redesigning the implementation to iterate values directly: two `for` loops carry integer positions and test only `i < j`. This preserves the full contract while eliminating symbolic indexing and its result-bearing abstraction entirely.
